  "description": "PERFORMANCE\n\nWe have developed the lightest possible bike to deliver outstanding performance. An agile climber that is suited to changes of speed and taking bends at top speeds.\n\nLIGHTNESS\n\nWe have fully optimised its thickness in critical areas and, with our Hollow Core Internal Moulding (HCIM) technology, we have maximised the stiffness of the carbon.\n\nAERO SHAPES AND MINIMISED TUBES\n\nDespite being a performance bike, its straight lines and Aero shapes follow the design principles of the Aerolight. The minimised tubes maintain the characteristic geometry and essence of a BH competition bike.\n\nAIR BOW FORK\n\nThe Air Bow has its own characteristic curved shape. The distance to the wheel is fully oversized, with no pressure zones where the air flows and vibrations from the asphalt are absorbed.\n\nRIGHT DOWN TO THE SMALLEST DETAIL\n\nHundreds of hours of computer-assisted analysis to fully integrate the components and eliminate any elements that slow you down. HIDDEN QUICK LEVERS; No need for tools, fully concealed and easy to use. NOT A CABLE IN SIGHT; A clean frame with 100% internal cabling. STEERING + HANDLEBARS; A steering + handlebars set that fits together to form a single block in the steering tube, maximising aerodynamics and air penetration.\n\nHIDDEN SEAT POST CLAMP SYSTEM\n\nIt is housed inside the seat tube for optimal aerodynamics and bike stiffness. Its tightening system in the lower part of the top tube is highly effective, with torque ranging from 3 Nm - 5 Nm.\n\nFINISHING TOUCHES ON THE ULTRALIGHT\n\nWe wanted to round off the Ultralight with a range of high-end accessories that fit the shape of the frame and maintain its aerodynamics. Toolbox, bottle and bottle holder & Planck rear light.",
